.TH BLITZLINE 1 "2026-10-18" "Blitzline" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blitzline \- turn a foreign-language recording into an Anki vocabulary deck
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blitzline check
.RB [ -l " " CODE ]
.RB [ --config " " FILE ]
.br
.B blitzline run
.I MEDIA
.RB [ -l " " CODE | --deck-profile " " NAME ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B blitzline resume
.I RUN_DIR
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B blitzline export
.I RUN_DIR
.B --format
.RI { apkg | tsv | anki }
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B blitzline clean
.I RUN_DIR
.RB [ --apply ]
.br
.B blitzline retry-stage
.I RUN_DIR
.B --stage
.I STAGE
.br
.B blitzline capabilities
.SH DESCRIPTION
Blitzline takes an audio or video recording, finds vocabulary in its
source-language transcript, chooses example sentences, cuts matching audio or
video clips, and prepares Anki cards. A run is the folder holding that work.
The folder also lets you continue after a stop. When inputs have not changed,
Blitzline reuses completed stages and successful model responses.
.PP
If you already have subtitles, give Blitzline the recording and its timed SRT
file
with
.BR --srt .
This skips transcription; WhisperX is only needed if you separately enable
audio re-listening. Without subtitles or timed ASR JSON, configure a
transcription backend first. Proofreading and translation are optional and off
by default; you can make a source-language deck without translating the
subtitles.
.SS Get ready
Install Blitzline with its APKG extra if you want a deck file that Anki can
import:
.PP
.nf
python3 -m pip install 'blitzline[apkg]'
.fi
.PP
Install FFmpeg, Blitzer
.RB ( bltzr ),
and a Blitzer language pack separately. A language code such as
.B slv
selects the pack; a deck profile selects that language and the Anki deck
together.
.PP
Create a TOML configuration file. This small example uses OpenRouter to review
Slovenian vocabulary and writes an APKG. Replace the model identifier with one
available to your account. Set
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
in your shell environment; the key itself does not belong in this file.
.PP
.nf
[llm]
review = "router"

[profiles.router]
provider = "openrouter"
model = "YOUR_MODEL_ID"
api_key_env = "OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
response_format = "json_object"

[export]
format = "apkg"

[decks.slovenian]
language = "slv"
deck = "Blitzline::Slovenian"
card_types = ["Sentence1", "Sentence2"]
.fi
.PP
Save it as
.B config.toml
for the commands below. Once it works, you can put it in your user config
directory and omit
.BR --config .
Use
.B blitzline check
to see which tools, deck profiles, and API-key environment variables Blitzline
can find. This check does not send a model request or test whether the key is
accepted by the provider.
.PP
.nf
blitzline check --config config.toml --language slv
.fi
.SS Make the deck
Suppose
.B recording.m4a
and
.B recording.sl.srt
contain the same recording in Slovenian. Run:
.PP
.nf
blitzline run recording.m4a --srt recording.sl.srt \\
  --config config.toml --deck-profile slovenian
.fi
.PP
Blitzline prints the run folder. When it finishes, look under that folder's
.B exports/apkg/
directory for
.BR cards.apkg .
In Anki, choose File, then Import, and select that APKG. If you prefer to stop
and inspect the vocabulary decisions before making clips, add
.B --stop-after review
to the run command, then continue with
.BR "blitzline resume RUN_DIR" .
An intentional stop may print
.B cards: 0
because cards are counted at export; it does not mean the review failed.
.SS What happens along the way
Progress lines follow the order of work: source checks, transcript import or
transcription, optional proofreading and translation, Blitzer vocabulary
extraction, model or manual vocabulary review, clip cutting, and export. The
run folder keeps reports for these stages. A progress line beginning with
.B Reusing
means Blitzline checked the saved result and did not perform that stage again.
.SS If the run needs attention
The run folder contains
.BR artifacts/05-review-report.json ,
which records vocabulary decisions and errors. If Blitzline asks for manual
review, compare that report with
.BR artifacts/04-vocabulary.json ,
edit
.BR artifacts/review.json ,
and pass the edited file explicitly:
.PP
.nf
blitzline resume RUN_DIR --review RUN_DIR/artifacts/review.json
.fi
.PP
If you did not configure an LLM for review, this editable-review path is the
normal route. If a command failed because of a transient problem, running
.B resume
again reuses valid earlier work. The word
.B Reusing
in progress output means that stage was recovered from the run folder.
.SS After checking the imported deck
You can preview removal of intermediate JSON, working clips, logs, and request
caches. The APKG stays in the run folder. Nothing is removed automatically when
export succeeds.
.PP
.nf
blitzline clean RUN_DIR
blitzline clean RUN_DIR --apply
.fi
.PP
The first command only lists the planned cleanup. Use the second only after
you have checked the imported deck: a cleaned run cannot be resumed or
re-exported. Cleanup requires a completed, verified APKG or TSV export.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "check " "[--language CODE] [--config FILE]"
Show configured tools, deck profiles, model profiles, and which key environment
variables are set. With a language code, also check that Blitzer can use that
language pack. No transcription or model request is made.
.TP
.BI "run " "MEDIA [OPTIONS]"
Start or reuse a run for the recording at
.IR MEDIA .
Supply a language with
.B --language
or choose a configured
.BR --deck-profile .
Use
.B --srt
or
.B --asr-json
when a transcript already exists.
.TP
.BI "resume " "RUN_DIR [OPTIONS]"
Continue a saved run. The directory is the one printed by
.BR run .
Saved settings are reused unless you explicitly pass
.B --config
or other override options.
.TP
.BI "export " "RUN_DIR --format {apkg|tsv|anki} [OPTIONS]"
Deliver validated cards from a completed media stage in another format.
.B apkg
creates an importable package;
.B tsv
creates tabular files and media;
.B anki
sends notes to a running Anki through AnkiConnect.
.TP
.BI "clean " "RUN_DIR [--apply]"
Preview cleanup of a completed portable export. With
.BR --apply ,
remove run intermediates and leave the verified export plus a small receipt.
Direct Anki delivery alone is not a portable export and cannot be cleaned this
way.
.TP
.BI "retry-stage " "RUN_DIR --stage STAGE"
Mark a failed, partial, or interrupted stage and its later stages for retry.
This command itself makes no model request; use
.B resume
afterward. Stage names include their numbers, for example
.BR 05-review .
.TP
.B capabilities
Print machine-readable JSON describing supported automation contracts.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Choosing inputs and locations
.TP
.BI "-l, --language " CODE
Use the three-letter lowercase Blitzer language code, such as
.BR slv .
Accepted by
.B run
and
.BR check .
For
.BR run ,
a selected deck profile can supply the language instead.
.TP
.BI "--deck-profile " NAME
Use a named
.B [decks.NAME]
profile from the configuration. It chooses the source language, destination
deck, and card types. Available on
.BR run ,
.BR resume ,
and
.BR export .
.TP
.BI "--config " FILE
Read the named TOML file. For
.BR run ,
the selection order is this option, then
.BR BLITZLINE_CONFIG ,
then the user config file. On
.B resume
and
.BR export ,
omit this option to reuse settings saved with the run. Relative paths inside
the TOML file are resolved from its directory.
.TP
.BI "--output " DIR
Put a new run in
.IR DIR .
Only
.B run
accepts this option. Without it, Blitzline chooses a run folder under the
user data directory and prints the full path.
.TP
.BI "--srt " FILE
Use an existing source-language SRT subtitle file with the recording. This
skips transcription. Available on
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.BI "--asr-json " FILE
Use an existing timed ASR JSON transcript instead of transcribing. Do not
combine with
.BR --srt .
.TP
.BI "--asr-backend " "{local|modal|http}"
Choose the transcription backend for this invocation. It is used only when
transcription or configured re-listening is needed. Local transcription uses
WhisperX; Modal and HTTP need their own configuration.
.TP
.BI "--review " FILE
Use edited vocabulary decisions from
.I FILE
instead of asking the review model. Usually this is an edited copy of
.BR artifacts/review.json .
.SS Processing and delivery
.TP
.BI "--stop-after " STAGE
Stop after
.BR transcript ,
.BR proofread ,
.BR translate ,
.BR vocabulary ,
.BR review ,
or
.BR media .
The CLI also accepts
.BR export ,
the final stage. Use
.B resume RUN_DIR
to continue. Available on
.B run
and
.BR resume .
.TP
.B --proofread, --no-proofread
Enable or disable model proofreading of the transcript. It requires a
configured proofreading profile when enabled. Off by default.
.TP
.B --translate, --no-translate
Enable or disable translation of subtitles into English. It requires a
configured translation profile when enabled. Off by default. Vocabulary card
meanings are handled by review and do not require this option.
.TP
.BI "--clips " "{audio|video}"
Choose the media attached to example cards. Video clips require a source with
video; the default is audio.
.TP
.BI "--format " "{apkg|tsv|anki}"
Choose the delivery format. On
.BR export ,
this option is required. On
.B run
or
.BR resume ,
it overrides the configured format. An APKG requires the optional
.B blitzline[apkg]
dependency; direct
.B anki
delivery requires AnkiConnect.
.TP
.B --allow-partial, --no-allow-partial
Allow or refuse delivery of accepted cards when some candidates or clips still
need attention. Refusing partial delivery is the default; the run keeps a
report of omitted items.
.SS Maintenance and general flags
.TP
.B --apply
With
.BR clean ,
perform the previewed removal of intermediates. Without it,
.B clean
changes nothing.
.TP
.BI "--stage " STAGE
With
.BR retry-stage ,
name the failed, partial, or interrupted stage to retry, such as
.BR 05-review .
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show short CLI help. Run it after a command, for example
.BR "blitzline run --help" ,
to see that command's flags.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed Blitzline version.
.SH FILES AND ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B User configuration
With an absolute
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
Blitzline looks for
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/blitzline/config.toml .
Otherwise it uses the platform's user config directory. An explicit
.B --config
or
.B BLITZLINE_CONFIG
takes precedence.
.TP
.B Default run location
With an absolute
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
new runs go under
.BR $XDG_DATA_HOME/blitzline/runs .
Otherwise Blitzline uses the platform's user data directory. An explicit
.B --output
takes precedence.
.TP
.B Run contents
.B artifacts/
holds stage results and reports;
.B media/
holds working example clips;
.B exports/
holds deliverables;
.B logs/
holds progress events;
.B .cache/
holds reusable responses;
.B manifest.json
records the run state. Keep these together until you are satisfied with the
export.
.TP
.B API keys
Provider profiles name an environment variable with
.BR api_key_env .
For the OpenRouter example above, set
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
before running review. Blitzline reports whether it is set but does not print
the key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command succeeded, including an intentional
.B --stop-after
or a cleanup preview.
.TP
.B 1
A stage, prerequisite, or external service failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command usage or configuration.
.TP
.B 3
The run needs review before delivery can continue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bltzr (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
Project setup and configuration examples are in the Blitzline documentation.
